  "conclusions": [
    "Schema gaps are real in selected schema1 records: no compatible AudioTracks, generated/global/colour/proxy settings, addressable property/graph/keyframe/caption state or per-object revision. Request extends same owner schema with explicit migration rather than defining competing B model.",
    "Model/edit rules are BCL, while only public Save/Load codecs are path-based and private strict JsonOptions uses unknown-member rejection. Portable same-codec/source-library request is a genuine owner boundary; extraction must preserve original validation/CAS/lock/Flush(true)/atomic move and revision rules.",
    "Existing integral-frame edits and shared rational MediaTimebase/MediaTimelineClip/MediaTimelineEdits exist; renderer projects same IDs/timebase into owner clips. Reusing them is appropriate; their presence does not implement full audio/visual/node catalog or UI/AI API parity.",
    "MotionMediaAssetReferences.RetainedSource refuses nonGUID FileID or missing retained revision. PreparedMediaAssetLease/MediaAssetPreparationService consume actual retained resolver/current actor, verify same retained identity/integrity under explicit byte budget, local-file materialization only, revalidate and dispose on owner scope. Fixture IDs/paths/IDB hashes cannot supply authority or an approved browser transport.",
    "MotionRenderService snapshots records before await, checks expected project revision and Files-returned asset/source revision, emits real JobID/ProjectID/SequenceID metadata, fixed WebmVp8 and disposes leases. This does not establish genuine backend availability/queue/formats/provider acceptance. Native render workflow fixture resolver is not maintained production Files authority.",
    "Request preserves engine-oriented acyclic boundaries: no Picture/Wave UI process dependency, no B private graphics/audio/node engine, and CUI typed shell/semantic action integration remains dependent on actual owner catalog.",
    "Pinned GStreamer83e7/GESfc343 binding plus old provenance is acknowledged as needing owner reconciliation/actual donor build evidence, not a source-only claim that full backend is available.",
    "All31 literal API rows retain unaccepted owner-extension state, and complete Motion section/acceptance remains active. Requested exhaustive typed operations/events/revisions/accessibility/platform/bootstrap requirements are not reduced to31 examples.",
    "Existing recorded original workflow1 local model/CLI/temp-file result is preserved with unknown assertion count; 24 return-code checkpoints are not24 tests and prove no browser/source/decode/render/hosted Files/full-model acceptance."
  ],
